      "answer": "All three analyses are done. Here's a summary:\n\n---\n\n### Sequence Statistics\n\n| Property | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Length | **18 bp** |\n| Type | DNA |\n| GC content | **50.0%** |\n| Base counts | A=4, C=4, G=5, T=5 |\n\n### ORF Search (both strands, min length 3)\n\n**No ORFs found.** The sequence contains a start codon (ATG) at position 1 but no in-frame stop codon in the forward direction, and no ATG-to-stop pattern on the reverse strand.\n\n### Translation (frame 1, standard genetic code)\n\nThe forward reading frame translates to a **6-residue peptide**:\n\n```\nATG CGT AAA CCC GGG TTT\n M   R   K   P   G   F\n```\n→ **`MRKPGF`** (no stop codon — the sequence ends before one is encountered)\n\n### Key takeaway\n\nThis 18-bp sequence is a complete open **reading frame fragment** (starts with Met but lacks a stop codon), so it would need additional downstream sequence to produce a full-length protein. The translated product `MRKPGF` is a short, arginine-lysine-rich peptide.",
